      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I believe what you're experiencing is the weird way parameters sync between platforms. To my knowledge, parameters sync based on their index in your Expression parameters, and not by name, unlike what has been officially stated. \nIf your Quest avatar lacks certain functionality that your PC avatar has, you need to ensure that the parameters for the things that it does have are in the same place as the PC counterpart. Since there usually shouldn't be any extra stuff the Quest version has over the PC one, copying the expression parameters asset for the Quest version should work fine. \nMy suggestion would be for VRC to instead sync parameters by name, which should retain backwards-compabitility with existing avatars, while making it simpler to create Quest compatible models. This is how it should have been from the start, I believe even Tupper mentioned that it was synced by name at some point.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-11-26T23:15:46.528Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Sending OSC data on PCVR (Facetracking in my case) to an avatar that is cross platform (has the animations setup to receive osc) causes the quest version to break and write to animations that are not my face tracking animations unless I upload an avatar that has the exact same FX animator. \nThis is a very game breaking bug, because often times the uploader won't notice and could be causing a ton of issues for quest players.\nIt also makes it impossible to use any other avatar on PC because the animators don't match.",
